  "title": "Missing faces and topological embeddings of sphere skeleta",
  "description": "<p>Let S be a finite simplicial triangulation of the topological sphere S^(2d), and let T be a missing d-face. We prove that adjoining T to the d-skeleton of S prevents a topological embedding in S^(2d). For d &gt;= 3, a graded Koszul calculation combines with established ambient-completion, anisotropy and metastable embedding theorems. For d = 2, we apply the Nevo-Wagner bistellar transfer theorem in the PL class supplied by the given triangulation: a contractible complementary manifold supplies the required disk map, and a flag subdivision supplies the base. This proves the statement of their Conjecture 1.3 without a standard PL structure assumption on the source. No claim of first priority or a new general method is made.</p><p>Unrefereed preprint. No independent human peer review has been obtained. AI tools were used extensively in solving, drafting, independently auditing, checking finite computations, and preparing the materials. AI-assisted review is not formal verification or independent human peer review. The accompanying verification programs supply bounded finite consistency evidence only; the universal conclusion is supported by the mathematical proof and its cited theorems.</p>",
